  "body": "### What changed\n- `AddTool::new` assigns the lowest unused controller number in `1-99999` (`tool_numbers::next_free`), stores it on `ToolDef::number`, and exposes `AddTool::number()`.\n- `ImportTools::with_options` allocates sequential unused numbers (`tool_numbers::next_free_from`) for every newly added or renamed tool while keeping existing and replaced tools' numbers reserved during the batch.\n- `project::apply::check_and_apply` freezes legacy unnumbered `EntityKind::Tool` records to their 1-based name-sorted list position on load without emitting load notes.\n- `SetToolNumber::new` refuses `None` by tool name so tools always keep an explicit number, while permitting the same number across disjoint setup machines (`setup_mount::machine_of`).\n- `tool_numbers::numbers` assigns the lowest unused number to any stray raw `ToolDef { number: None }` entity so unnumbered test fixtures never collide with numbered tools.\n- `add_tool` returns `number` and `posts_as` over MCP, UI add status displays `(T{number})`, `tool_settings` clamps existing tools to `1..=MAX`, `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md` documents the updated MCP contract, and `examples/catalog/2d/first-part/build.camscript` adds its tools in `T1`/`T2`/`T3` order.\n\n### Cause\n- `AddTool` and `ImportTools` left `ToolDef::number` as `None`.\n- `tool_numbers::numbers` fell back to each unnumbered tool's 1-based index in `model::named_entities`, so adding, renaming, or deleting a tool renumbered other tools between posts.\n\n### Tests\n- Pinning tests (red on `upstream/main`, green after fix):\n  - `tool_numbers::adding_an_earlier_sorting_tool_keeps_posted_t_and_h_words`\n  - `tool_numbers::deleting_an_earlier_tool_keeps_remaining_posted_t_and_h_words`\n  - `tool_numbers::legacy_unnumbered_project_keeps_posted_numbers_after_add_and_delete`\n  - `tool_numbers::importing_earlier_sorting_tool_keeps_existing_numbers`\n- Mutation checks:\n  - Reverted `AddTool::apply` to `number: None`: `adding_an_earlier_sorting_tool_keeps_posted_t_and_h_words` failed (red), then passed on restore (green).\n  - Reverted `ImportTools::apply` `Step::Add` to `number: None`: `tool_import_modes::update_adds_unmatched_and_skips_identical_in_one_undo` failed (red), then passed on restore (green).\n  - Reverted `project/apply.rs` to `upstream/main`: `legacy_unnumbered_project_keeps_posted_numbers_after_add_and_delete` failed (red), then passed on restore (green).\n  - Reverted `commands/tool_number.rs` to `upstream/main`: `tool_numbers::a_number_is_set_refused_to_clear_and_walked_by_undo_and_redo` and `setup_mounts_post::a_tool_number_shared_across_machines_posts_but_clashes_within_one` failed (red), then passed on restore (green).\n- Gate after review fix (`f1ed9b6e7aa1a4ea39a8ca14047c3d0ce11a47e8`):\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 92/93 steps passed, 11.2 minutes. The sole failure is the existing #2483 Linux wrap motion-line-count mismatch (`3246 != 3245`). The new tool-number pin and indexed fixture test pass. Across suites: 2,360 passed, 1 failed, 18 ignored.\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed with no warnings.\n\n### Goldens moved\n- None (`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty).\n- `examples/catalog/2d/first-part/build.camscript` reorders `add_tool` calls to match the committed `first-part.nc` tool numbers (`DR-0600` T1, `EM-0600-4FL` T2, `EM-1000-4FL` T3).\n\n### Not exercised\n- `cargo xtask gate batch` was not run after the final edit (all 27 golden `.nc` suites ran cleanly prior to reverting an intermediate `wrap_rotary_parallel_microarc4.nc` edit, and `example_catalog` + `first_4axis_part` + `first_router_part` passed).\n- The full wrapped microARC golden test has the existing Linux motion-line-count failure tracked by #2483. The wrap fixture now explicitly preserves the committed tool table: `BN 1/8` T1, `EM 1/4 3FL` T2, `EM 1/8 2FL` T3. `wrapped_fixture_keeps_golden_tool_numbers` pins all posted tool comments and T/H lines independently of motion-line count. Removing that fixture table fails the pin; restoring it passes. The indexed microARC program also passes unchanged.\n\n### Overlaps\n- Touches different functions or lines in files also edited by `#2236`, `#2092`, `#2253`, `#2448`, `#2024`, `#2149`, `#2134`, `#2256`, `#2370`, `#2185`, `#1798`, `#1330`, and `#1713`; whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nProcess change: yes\nChangelog: Assign stable lowest-unused tool numbers at tool creation, import, and legacy project load (#2442)\n\n\n### UI before and after (review finding 2)\n\nReal UI renders of the same catalog tool added through the UI command queue, then opened in the tool editor. The before image uses the parent product sources. The after image uses this PR's product sources. Images live only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch.\n\nBefore: tool number `0` means list position; add status has no T number.\n\n![Before: tool number editor and add status](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/413bf75d50bb172d460f393f995634991ca64d1d/2488/tool-number-before.png)\n\nAfter: tool number `1` is explicit; add status shows `(T1)`.\n\n![After: tool number editor and add status](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/413bf75d50bb172d460f393f995634991ca64d1d/2488/tool-number-after.png)\n\nThe temporary capture assertions checked the editor label and add-status number. The after assertions failed against the parent product sources and passed after restoration. The capture harness and evidence were removed from the PR worktree before the gate.\n\nFixes #2442\n",
